WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:18.760
Greenland the largest island in the world a&nbsp;
nice desert at the mercy of the ocean lashed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:25.560
by Arctic winds populated by Seals and polar&nbsp;
bears where time seems to have stopped flowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.720
but beyond that what do we really know about&nbsp;
Greenland? We came here with very specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:37.400
purposes to dispel hard to die myths to tell&nbsp;
you the parable of an inhospitable land shaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:42.640
by Colonial domination that aspires to be&nbsp;
a nation to show you how this is not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.400
a white spot drawn on a map but rather&nbsp;
a part of our history as human beings.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:59.920
Welcome to Greenland.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.600
for nearly four centuries settlers traded walrus&nbsp;
tusks and seal skins with Iceland and Norway in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.720
exchange for food wood and iron tools. At the&nbsp;
time however the Norse villages in Greenland were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:32.240
already falling into ruin. Within a few decades&nbsp;
nothing more was known of the inhabitants. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:37.280
crown of Copenhagen interested in keeping the&nbsp;
Artic trade routs active and hunting whales,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:43.560
in order to undermine the then Dutch competition&nbsp;
tried to reestablish contacts with the Lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:51.160
Colony. 300 years of inconclusive expeditions&nbsp;
followed until in 1721 the Lutheran pastor Hans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:56.400
Egede landed where the first Danish settlement&nbsp;
in Greenland would be born: Godthab... Good Hope

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:24.880
since 1979 Godthab has been renamed nuuk which&nbsp;
means cape and it's the capital of Greenland at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:30.560
that time aged believed not only that he would&nbsp;
meet survivors but also that these having been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:37.080
isolated for centuries still preached Catholicism&nbsp;
or paganism and that they spoke a some form of Old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:48.520
Norse. Egede was wrong. The Greenland coasts had&nbsp;
now become home to another people... The Inuit.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:54.880
the term Inuit, in the singular inuk, means&nbsp;
people and has replaced the derogatory and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:03:01.720
erroneous Eskimos which means those who wears no&nbsp;
shoes. These Arctic people descend from the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:07.840
Siberian men who migrated over the millennia to&nbsp;
the Northern areas of Alaska Canada and Greenland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:13.480
and have always lived by fishing and hunting&nbsp;
animals, such as polar bears seals reindeer and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:19.640
whales. Today 90% of greenlanders are Inuit&nbsp;
and largely speak the Kalaallisut language,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.320
which is completely different from&nbsp;
the European ones. In some Villages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:29.680
like in Tasiilaq, on the East Coast, the&nbsp;
Inuit have never abandoned their roots.

00:03:55.116 --> 00:04:01.880
Thule, the most direct ancestors of the Inuit,&nbsp;
penetrated Southwest Greenland around the 14th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:07.040
century, there is when the Nordic Atlantic&nbsp;
area was hit by a phenomenal climate known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:12.880
as the little Ice Age which is believed to have&nbsp;
caused The Disappearance of the Norse colonies. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:19.000
Godthab, Egede's mission was to convert the locals&nbsp;
which were perceived as Savages it was a slow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:26.160
process hindered by the presence of the Angakkuit,&nbsp;
the so-called Inuit shamans, who are seen as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:31.840
holders of knowledge in both the religion and&nbsp;
medical fields however the Danes began to populate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:37.760
the western coast, expanded Godthab and founded&nbsp;
the harbor of Jakobshavn, the modern Ilulissat.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:45.360
With the creation of the royal greenlandic&nbsp;
company in 1774 Copenhagen established a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:51.960
monopoly aimed at acquiring in exchange for coffee&nbsp;
and tobacco meat leather and handcraft products&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:58.680
including "Tupilac", bone statuettes depicting&nbsp;
demons from Inuit mythology. Thus by changing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:04.520
perspective the units began to deprive themselves&nbsp;
of resources that had always been necessary to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:10.840
their subsistence and access Western Market logic.&nbsp;
This trend was frowned upon by Danish officials,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:16.120
who feared that the Inuits would soon lose&nbsp;
their essence and therefore their usefulness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:22.840
Furthermore in 1814 Denmark was forced to cede&nbsp;
Norway to Sweden after being defeated in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:28.960
Napoleonic Wars and to rely only on the Icelandic&nbsp;
and greenlandic colonies. Then the presumed desire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:35.280
to preserve the Inuit culture was accompanied&nbsp;
by the need to make it more efficient. In 1835&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:40.600
the Royal company suggested building wooden&nbsp;
houses to replace the traditional Inuit homes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:46.520
there is huts and summer tents made of bones and&nbsp;
fabrics. Although famous the igloos were nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:52.080
more than shelters used for hunting and fishing&nbsp;
and although it is redundant to underline it...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:58.720
no, no single Inuk still lives in the igloos.&nbsp;
In 1856 the colonial administrators decreed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:03.880
that each settlement would have to elect its&nbsp;
own representatives in charge of supervising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:09.760
the society. However only the most experienced&nbsp;
hunters could carry out this task. In other words&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:15.560
the Royal company delegitimized the Angakkuit,&nbsp;
the shamans, and destabilized a proven social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:29.400
structure. The same thing happened when Denmark&nbsp;
decided to claim greenand in its entirety.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:57.680
shortly thereafter the advancement of European&nbsp;
claims on the Arctic routes and the outbreak of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:03.280
the two World Wars would have made Greenland&nbsp;
geostrategic potential evident. In 1941 with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:08.480
Copenhagen occupied by the Nazi army, the&nbsp;
Danish ambassador to Washington, Henry Kaufman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:13.680
allowed the United States to establish five&nbsp;
temporary military bases on the island. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:19.200
gave an important tactical advantage to the Allied&nbsp;
Air Force. However once the conflict was over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:24.440
the White House didn't give up, in fact&nbsp;
the United States aspired to exploit the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:29.680
island for an anti-soviet purpose and to take&nbsp;
possession of cryolite, a mineral use for for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:35.280
the manufacturing of aluminium present on&nbsp;
the south coast. In great secrecy in 1951,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:42.320
American Engineers began to build a gigantic Air&nbsp;
Base in Thule, still operating today. In 1968 the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:47.640
crash of an American fighter caused the dispersion&nbsp;
of four tactical thermonuclear bombs ,which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:53.200
exploded and contaminated the entire Thuli area&nbsp;
one of the four warheads is still missing today.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:58.680
But 2 years before this incident, Washington had&nbsp;
decommissioned another Secret Base, Camp Century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:04.520
which was supposed to host 600 nuclear missiles&nbsp;
capable of reaching Moscow. These US military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:11.160
projects forced the local Inuit communities to&nbsp;
move even 100 km away. At the same time the noise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:16.800
and the clangs of the machines irreparably&nbsp;
affected ecosystems that had until then been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:23.560
immersed in silence. In any case Greenland's&nbsp;
most important resource still remains the sea.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:45.640
Already in the first half of the 20th century&nbsp;
in Copenhagen they had noticed how the fishing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:51.440
of shrimps, halibut, cod and salmon could&nbsp;
generate much greater profits than those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:57.840
deriving from traditional seal or reindeer&nbsp;
hunting. In 1953 driven by decolonization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:02.400
the Danish government elevated Greenland to&nbsp;
the status of an autonomous Province. Over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:09.200
the course of 20 years Copenhagen launched&nbsp;
two development plans called G50 and G60,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:13.760
aimed at modernizing the Island's fishing&nbsp;
industry and settlements. These welfare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:29.120
policies have certainly improved&nbsp;
the quality of Greenlandic life.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:55.440
Despite its obvious advantages, modernization&nbsp;
brought about much larger and more sudden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:00.040
upheavals than those suffered previously.&nbsp;
The abolition of the monopoly of the royal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:05.960
Greenland company and the construction of New Port&nbsp;
facilities removed the social role of the hunter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:12.040
who until 50 years earlier colonial officials&nbsp;
had considered the Pinnacle of Inuk society.&nbsp;

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:17.000
To guarantee greater productivity of the&nbsp;
locals now employed in the fish factories, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:22.520
urbanization projects involved the forced movement&nbsp;
of thousands of people from the villages to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:29.240
new Urban centers inhabited, this time equipped&nbsp;
with shops schools and hospitals. Apart from from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:35.120
barracks and wooden buildings Nuuk is today&nbsp;
the emblem of an accelerated development that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:40.520
doesn't take into consideration the lifestyle of&nbsp;
the Inuits. Just think of the so-called block P,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:46.560
an abnormal ghetto residential structure built in&nbsp;
the 60s, now demolished which was said to contain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:53.160
1% of the entire greenlandic population. Thanks&nbsp;
to the opportunities that opened up on the island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:59.400
Inuits found themselves busy with tasks they had&nbsp;
never done before. However they were paid 25% %&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:05.080
less than Danes in the same positions. To earn&nbsp;
an equivalent salary an Inuk had to have lived at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:11.240
least 10 years in Denmark. Economic discrimination&nbsp;
went hand in hand with some perverse intentions:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:17.000
in 1951 the Danish authorities took 22&nbsp;
init children away from their families,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:21.800
to send them to Denmark and train them as&nbsp;
the future greenlandic ruling class. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:27.240
experiment needless to say failed. Half&nbsp;
of those children died at a young age and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:32.840
half were affected by mental disorder. Between&nbsp;
the 60s and' 70s, under government directives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:37.480
Danish doctors placed intrauterine coils&nbsp;
(contraceptive instruments) in the bodies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:42.680
of approximately 4,000 Inuit women and&nbsp;
girls. In doing so in just a few years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:48.600
the greenlandic birth rate, considered excessively&nbsp;
high at the time, was halved. The criticism and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:54.240
discontent towards the entire postcolonial system&nbsp;
led to the birth of the autonomous parliament of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.240 --> 00:12:01.200
Nuuk in 1979. Greenland chose its current flag in&nbsp;
1985, the same year it left the European economic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:06.920
Community (to protect its waters from the probable&nbsp;
siege of foreign fishing boats). In fact today&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:12.800
Greenland is not part of the European Union and&nbsp;
has enjoyed an autonomous government since 2009.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:17.880
Nonetheless the fate of the largest island in the&nbsp;
world is undefined. According to United Nations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:22.920
Greenlandic society suffers from the lack of&nbsp;
adequate housing and Healthcare facilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:28.880
It suffers from an educational system that&nbsp;
allows young people to emancipate themselves.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:46.920
In 2014 the Nuuk government created a&nbsp;
Reconciliation Commission, in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:51.960
heal relations with Denmark. It will be a long&nbsp;
process that will require the acquisition of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:57.720
greater awareness both on the part of the&nbsp;
Inuit community and the Danish authorities.

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:03.360
myself having lived here for nearly 1 and&nbsp;
1/2 years I've only experienced like one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:06.760
episode of a drunk person coming up&nbsp;
and saying I should go back where I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:12.120
came from uh I've heard other stories where&nbsp;
people got confronted during a night out or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:16.960
at a concert also being asked to go home&nbsp;
but I would say like in general people I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:21.760
meet are very open and honest that's&nbsp;
the thing about Greenlandic people.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:26.240
The wounds of the colonial&nbsp;
period perhaps have never healed.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:14:52.720
For the lower social classes, I think, most of&nbsp;
the stuff that I experience, alcoholism is a big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:59.720
problem like the social evolution kinda happened&nbsp;
too fast so to speak uh a lot of people lost their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:05.320
jobs because they had to be moved out of the&nbsp;
smaller cities into like Nuuk. There are like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:10.600
a couple of think we call them the blocks at the&nbsp;
you can't really see them here like where people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:17.720
got lodged in together and I think forcing a&nbsp;
person who his whole life has gone fishing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:22.200
gone hunting, to suddenly work in a factory&nbsp;
is kind of soul sucking in a weird way I could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:30.120
imagine that and also having access to alcohol&nbsp;
kind of messed a lot of people up I would imagine.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:35.680
The issues of greenlandic society do not&nbsp;
end here at all and now more than ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:40.760
in a 21st century marked by uncertainty&nbsp;
and competition between Global Powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:45.920
Greenland is destined to deal with the&nbsp;
inevitability of the future and its challenges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:58.600
its opportunities. But we will talk&nbsp;
more about this in the next video.

